<title>FRANCE: French adj June current a/c surplus 8.18 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French adj June current a/c surplus 8.18 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 8.18 billion francs in June, up from a revised 6.91 billion May, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>It originally said the current account registered a 6.98 billion franc surplus in May.</p>
<p>The ministry said that the seasonally adjusted surplus in the first six months of 1996 was 58.47 billion francs, compared with a 60.13 billion surplus in the same period a year earlier. Detailed figures in billions of francs showed:</p>
<p>					 Jun	May	Apr</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)    8.18     6.91     4.56</p>
<p> Current account		   3.19     8.60     4.47</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 6.78     6.95     5.15</p>
<p> Services			    7.84     3.81     6.54</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.50     0.40     0.40</p>
<p> Income			     -4.93     2.82    -3.37</p>
<p> Transfers			  -6.99    -5.37    -4.26</p>
<p>The ministry also gave the following seasonally adjusted data on the current account in billions of francs:</p>
<p>					 Jun	May	Apr</p>
<p> Current account		   8.18     6.91     4.56</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 7.36    10.23    -0.30</p>
<p> Services			    5.50     4.49     6.26</p>
<p>  -Travel			    4.09     4.14     4.43</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.48     0.46     0.45</p>
<p> Income			     -6.88     1.52     4.65</p>
<p>  -Investment income	    -6.36     0.46     0.68</p>
<p> Transfers			  -0.52    -0.52    -0.61</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
